sharpeRratio-fortran is a modern Fortran computational translation of
sharpeRratio 1.4.3 by Damien Challet.

Upstream package:
  sharpeRratio: Moment-Free Estimation of Sharpe Ratios
  Copyright (C) Damien Challet
  License field: GPL

This translation is distributed under GPL-3.0-only. The complete upstream
source is retained under original/sharpeRratio-master and its supplied archive
is retained under provenance/sharpeRratio-master.zip.

The package vendors the supplied ghyp-fortran translation, derived from ghyp
1.6.5 by Marc Weibel, David Luethi, and Henriette-Elise Breymann. ghyp and its
Fortran translation are GPL-2.0-or-later. Their notices and license are retained
under provenance.

The spline calibration coefficients are exact IEEE binary64 values extracted
from the upstream R serialized data objects a, a_medium, and f. The extraction
script is retained under provenance/extract_calibration.py.
